# 03-db.mdc

Database and migration conventions.

- Model prediction-market entities explicitly (`market`, `trade`, `position`).
- Make migrations additive and reversible; do not rewrite existing auth/user tables.
- Store credits, shares, pools, and payouts as integers.
- Store sufficient audit data to reconstruct trade history and P/L.
- Seed exactly the demo markets needed for the public flow unless the user asks for more.
- Prefer explicit indexes for market status and user-position lookups.
- Avoid destructive schema or data operations unless the user explicitly approves them.
